  "design_notes": [
    "The table heading says the RCS is \"used in space\". The table has no twin, fact, cost or mass column, so those fields are absent.",
    "Isp is stored without the \"~\" and tagged real_world_approximate: the three figures are typical of the real thruster classes.",
    "\"Cheap\", \"costly\", \"weak\", \"limited fuel\", \"toxic\" and \"complex\" have no numbers. The ones Core could act on are flags; the design gives no cost for any RCS option, so the cost words cannot affect the budget yet.",
    "Helium Shortage (6.8) is weighted by \"pressure-fed systems\", but the design labels no part as pressure-fed, so no RCS option carries that anomaly weight (same choice as upper_stage_engine.json). Real hydrazine and bipropellant thrusters are fed by tank pressure, so they are the natural candidates once the design names them.",
    "No option is restricted to a contract."
  ],
